In article <T36273C.89Jun2025424@saha.saha.hut.FI> t36273c@saha.saha.hut.FI (Ari Huttunen) writes:
>Ever considered putting in graves in nethack? Some of the graves could be
>of previous players.. You could find valuable possessions there.. But you
>would need a shovel, of course, to get it up! Digging a grave open would also
>make the Gods angry. AND you cold make a new monster 'Carrion crawler' that
>could dig the graves open..

>Now, don't ask me who buried him...

This is exactly what my question would be.  I think ghosts and their hoardes
of [cursed] treasure pretty much foot the bill.  Perhaps you might find a
corpse near the ghosts sometime, but this would be for effect only, not for
any good reason, and so is probably unecessary.  

What I think we could use is some other mechanism for raising luck points.
Does sacrifice (which I don't have in my version) do this?  Are that and
tossing gems at unicorns the only way.  The reason I ask is, sometimes I go
through whole games without ever seeing a unicorn, and playing with bad luck
(especially if you had no choice, i.e. you kill Fido by accident, etc.) is
really hard.  I'm not saying it should be *easy* to raise you luck, but having
a few different (albeit tricky) mechanisms would at least give you some
options.

Just wond'ring aloud...

